k legs sit off  another thing i just have to chime in is  make sure you put your curtains  like a foot out from your windows  because otherwise you're going to block  all your lighting  and to me that's a cardinal rule go out  a foot on either side and then when you  open all the fabric that's covering it  you have your whole windows  exactly you guys also have a lighting  tip i am all ears for this because  lighting changes everything  um you'll notice we added a mirror over  the fireplace we added sconces  a different fixture over the um over the  dining room table  and we mixed it because the furniture  that we were looking at has a lot of  rich textures  so the lighting can have a shine  it can have different you can mix  metallics that was one of your questions  i know  yes but um always mix metals and you  want to be able to control the mood  in the space so we've got a table lamp  um the cord runs underneath the rug and  gets plugged into the wall  there's a floor lamp um there's little  sconces next to the fireplace  but you want to be able to control the  mood you don't want overhead lighting on  necessarily if you're having a intimate  chat  or if you're watching television or  reading now nate and jeremiah you also  added a bunch of final touches  um let's take a look at that oh gosh  that looks so you can really see the  space starts to come alive here the tv  is concealed it's not really the focal  point of the room anymore  um but it's still fully functioning you  know for us greenery  branches pottery that is always kind of  that that final layer to any space and  it really brings that outdoors in  um and it really makes the space really  evolved and again like people are living  there and it brings that warmth  tierra were you saying that you're kind  of starting from scratch here  like you don't have a ton of stuff  you're starting you want to start fresh  correct i just moved and this is my old  furniture and i wanted to just start  over  so this i